<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>1.</strong><strong>Auxiliary
boiler feed water pump breaker faulty</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Breaker is
tripping. It is not holding at ON position.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Operate the system
with the standby pump. Isolate the faulty breaker &amp; change with new one.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>2. Auxiliary boiler feed water pump over
current trip</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Pump is drawing
high current &amp; over current relay is tripping the breaker.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Isolate the pump and rotate the shaft by hand. Check
for possible reason of tight rotation. Check line valves.</li><li>Check the electrical circuit for any possible fault.</li></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>3. Auxiliary boiler feed water pump break
down</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Low feed water
pressure alarm. Pump is not building pressure.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Change over to
another pump if it is not started on auto and confirm line valves are correctly
set. Overhaul the defective pump after isolation.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>4. Auxiliary boiler High salinity in feed
water</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">High salinity
alarm.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Blow down the
water. Check for sea water ingress in the system and rectify same before
putting the boiler back in operation.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>5. Auxiliary boiler feed water turbine pump
breakdown</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Low feed water
pressure alarm. Pump is not building pressure.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Check the valve
status &amp; cascade tank level. Overhaul the pump if necessary.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>6. Auxiliary boiler feed water auto
controller is not working</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Boiler water level
not maintained as per consumption requirements. Level will come down &amp; may
result in shut down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Change over to
manual line. Overhaul the control.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>7. Auxiliary boiler water level remote gauge
not working</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Water level gauge
in ECR(Engine Control Room) will show error leading to wrong information.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Check water level from local gauge glass.</li><li>Rectify remote gauge glass error.</li></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>8. Auxiliary boiler igniter transformer is
not working</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Boiler will not
fire and will trip on flame failure.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Replace the
transformer and put the boiler back in use ONLY after rectifying fault.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>9. Auxiliary boiler smoke side dirty</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Boiler steam production rate will reduce.</li><li>Fuel oil consumption will increase.</li><li>Smoke density increase causing port authorities to
stop all the operations related to the boiler.</li></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Soot blow the auxiliary boiler regularly.</li><li>Manual cleaning of smoke side as per vessels trading
pattern.</li></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>10. Auxiliary boiler Auto combustion control
failure</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Causes:</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Auxiliary boiler is
not firing on auto.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Remedial Actions:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Change burner control to manual mode&amp; fire the
boiler on manual.</li><li>Keep in mind all alarms and cut outs may not be be in functional in this mode. </li></ul>

